<title>USA: Watsco to buy two Carrier distributors.</title>
<headline>Watsco to buy two Carrier distributors.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Watsco Inc said on Tuesday that it has entered into a letter of intent with Carrier Corp, a subsidiary of United Technologies Corp, to acquire the net assets and business of two Carrier distribution operations.</p>
<p>The operations, Comfort Products and Central Plains, sell air conditioning and heating equipment under the &quot;Carrier&quot; and &quot;Bryant&quot; brand names and together reported 1995 revenues of about $60 million.</p>
</text>
